{"questions":[{"question_id":"shaQfGQgffjfRATa","paperTitle":"AIEEE 2002","year":2002,"examDate":2002,"subject":"mathematics","chapter":"permutations-and-combinations","chapterGroup":"algebra","topic":"conditional-permutations","type":"mcq","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"five-digit-number-divisible-by-3-is-formed-using-0-1-2-3-4-a-jee-main-2002-marks-4-shaqfgqgffjfrata.htm","content":"Five digit number divisible by 3 is formed using 0, 1, 2, 3, 4 and 5 without repetition. Total number of such numbers are :","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"312"},{"identifier":"B","content":"3125"},{"identifier":"C","content":"120"},{"identifier":"D","content":"216"}],"correct_options":["D"],"explanation":"<b>Note :</b> For a number to be divisible by 3, the sum of digits should be divisible by 3.\n<br><br>Here given numbers are 0, 1, 2, 3, 4 and 5. Out of those 6 numbers possible sets of 5 numbers are (1, 2, 3, 4, 5) and (0, 1, 2, 4, 5) whose sum are divisible by 3.\n<br><br><b>Set 1 :</b> Set is = (1, 2, 3, 4, 5). Sum of digits = 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 5 = 15 (Divisible by 3)\n<br><br><img class=\"question-image\" src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/o8KOhIH29o7j9qnK0/anP0DFZ8yzpMUikYtaGZ4IKXkuPX9/u4pypGVuaFuCUFJVKHufTs/image.png\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"AIEEE 2002 Mathematics - Permutations and Combinations Question 218 English Explanation 1\">\n<br><br>So total no of arrangement = 1<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0.02ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.09ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -491 778 482\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>2<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertica